2)	Project Title and Description

LeaseUpNoles - a Tallahassee-focused web app where FSU students can search off-campus housing by price and straight-line distance to campus, and read reviews left by other students who've actually lived there

3)	Accomplishments and overall project status during this increment 
During this increment, our team focused on setting up the project infrastructure and planning the development work. We created the lease-up-noles GitHub repository and gave every team member access, so everyone can contribute through the same codebase.
We then reviewed our proposed scope and broke it into GitHub issues covering the features and setup tasks needed to deliver the app. Once the full list of issues was finalized, we divided them among team members so that each person has clear responsibilities and the work is spread evenly.
We also completed the backend setup in Supabase. The project was created under the lease-up-noles organization on the Free plan, hosted in the East US (Ohio) region, with Postgres and Authentication enabled. Team members were invited to the project with Developer access so everyone can work with the database directly.
Overall, the project is on track with our initial scope. The groundwork is in place: version control, a defined and assigned backlog, and a working backend environment. Our remaining setup tasks are to configure environment variables locally and in Vercel and to verify the connection with a test query. Once those are complete, we will move into building core features such as listing search, filtering, and student reviews.
4)	Challenges, changes in the plan and scope of the project and things that went wrong during this increment

Challenges: Setup was initially challenging due to task dependencies. We handled this by tracking the dependency explicitly in GitHub and prioritizing Issue #1 so the blocked tasks can move forward as soon as it's done. Going through the backlog together and tracking ownership in GitHub Issues made it clear who is responsible for what.

Changes in plan or scope: There were no changes to the project's scope during this increment. The features we proposed are still our target.

Things that went wrong: Nothing major went wrong. The only setback was that the Supabase integration could not be fully verified this increment because it is waiting on the scaffold.

