6)	Plans for the next increment
In the next increment, our team plans to move from setup into building the core features of the application. First, we will finish the project scaffold (Issue #1), which unblocks the remaining setup work. We will then configure environment variables locally and in Vercel and run a test query to confirm the app can communicate with our Supabase database.
Once the foundation is in place, we will design and create the database tables for listings, users, and reviews. 

7)	Stakeholder Communication
To our stakeholders,
Here's a brief update on Lease Up Noles, our platform to help FSU students find off-campus housing in Tallahassee and share honest reviews of where they've lived.
Progress so far
We've focused on building a strong foundation. Our six-person team now has a shared workspace, and we've divided the project into clearly assigned tasks. We've also finished setting up secure storage for listings, student accounts, and reviews, with built-in account protection.
Where we stand
We're on track with our original goals. Students will be able to search listings by rent, bedrooms, and distance to campus, and to read and write reviews. No planned features have been cut.
A small delay
We can't confirm that the website and its data storage are working together until the website's basic structure is finished. Software projects often have this kind of sequencing, much like an electrical inspection has to wait until a building is framed. It's our top priority, and we don't expect it to affect the overall timeline.
Next steps
•	Finish the website's structure and confirm everything connects
•	Enable student accounts and login
•	Build search with price, bedroom, and distance filters
•	Begin the student review feature
If you have insight into what students value most when choosing housing, we'd love to hear it as we set priorities.
Best regards,
The Lease Up Noles Team

